{
 "formatVersion": 1,
 "source": {
  "what": "Which colour variant each species takes, and whether it is set by the parent star class or by a material on the body.",
  "status": "Community knowledge, not a proprietary dataset — the same tables the codex teaches anyone who scans enough plants.",
  "transcribedFrom": "https://ed-dsn.net/en/exobiological-flora/ (retrieved 2026-09-11), to save typing several hundred rows by hand.",
  "verifiedAgainst": "CMDR FALrenica's own journals: 235 star-table predictions correct and none wrong, and in all 47 material rows the colour he found was among the candidates.",
  "gameCodex": "bySpecies rebuilt 2026-09-26 from the game's own codex list (every variant's symbol and English name, as published by Canonn's codex reference). ED-DSN had 3 wrong rows (Fumerola carbosis tin; Recepta deltahedronix mercury and molybdenum) and 36 missing; genus tables (byGenus) now only cover species the list does not name."
 },
 "verification": {
  "againstOwnerJournals": "235 star-table predictions correct, 0 wrong, 23 classes blank; 47 of 47 material rows had the observed colour among the candidates.",
  "materialTieBreak": "Withdrawn 2026-09-22. An EDDN capture of 25,858 bodies carries 14,502 codex entries whose variant suffix names the deciding material outright; on the 907 bodies where more than one of a species' own materials was present, the rarest won 445 and lost 462. A fixed per-species priority fails too — every species shows contradictory pairs. It is not a ranking of the materials at all, so both candidates are offered again. The earlier 14-of-15 came from a single commander's 15 finds."
 },
